      "knowledge_point_id": "2954b59f-d701-502f-963b-b62098a87c34",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Sum to Infinity of a Geometric Series Expressed Using Decimals",
      "problem": "Calculate the sum to infinity of the geometric series $6.4+4.8+3.6+2.7+⋯$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=6.4$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{4.8}{6.4}=0.75.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.4}{1-0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.4}{0.25} \\\\  & =25.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
